      "content": "Thanks, this is a great start. The framing on the burn rate is exactly the kind of professional polish I need.\n\nI want to double-check the core tech before I finalize the appendix. I was just looking at the enzyme stability CSV—specifically the trial data for the new synthesized batch. The pitch deck they provided claims a 92% stability retention rate, which is incredible. But when I'm looking at the actual raw data points in those stability coefficient tables, the mean for several trial runs seems to be hovering around 55%.\n\nThat's a pretty massive gap between the pitch and the raw numbers. When you were doing your deep dive into those lab results, did you catch that discrepancy? I want to make sure I'm not misinterpreting the data before I present it.",
